title: The Price of Bread
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and c_prices_timer <= 0 and (year >= 1922 or inflation >= 30)
on-arrival: {!
Q.c_prices_timer = 4;
Q.month_actions += 1;
RG.target('militancy');
!}
frequency: 250
is-card: true
tags: movement

= The Price of Bread

[? if inflation < 60 : The mark is sliding. Wages are renegotiated every month, and every month they buy less. ?][? if inflation >= 60 : The mark is collapsing. Workers are paid twice a day and run to the shops before the prices change again. ?] In the markets, traders hold back butter and potatoes for a better price, and the women in the queues know it.

In **[+ sys_target_name +]** the queues are longest and angriest.

- @committees: Elect price control committees in the markets.
- @seize: Open the hoarders' warehouses in [+ sys_target_name +].
- @wages: Demand wages that rise with prices, with the unions.
- @easy_discard

@committees
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Slow, and it reaches every town.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids council work.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_councils == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.worker_support += 5;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

Committees of workers and housewives walk the markets with notebooks. Traders caught hoarding find their names in the party paper.

@seize
subtitle: Bread today in one district, and the police there tomorrow. The district may come out on strike.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district(Q.sys_target, {militancy: 10, repression: 8});
if (Q.sys_target_striking == 0 && Q.sys_target_militancy >= 55 && Math.random() < 0.5) {
    RG.startStrike(Q.sys_target);
}
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

A crowd opens a potato warehouse and sells its contents at last month's prices, paying the owner in cash. The owner calls the police anyway.

@wages
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A joint demand with the unions and the SPD.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any deal with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.spd_relation += 5;
Q.worker_support += 2;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

Wages tied to the cost of living: the demand is so obvious that the union leaders cannot refuse to sign it, though they would like to.
